       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, and I shouldn't have offered to earlier. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum recommended adult dose. Doses above 3,200 mg/day add no benefit and substantially raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. I can't think of an indication where that dose is appropriate, so a note on the order wouldn't make it safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf there's a clinical reason for going higher, such as a specific protocol, I'd suggest talking to pharmacy first. They can verify it and enter it through the appropriate channel. If there's a different intended dose or a different drug, tell me and I'll enter it."
